/* PARKED 2026-09-10 — first opening of main's last un-opened wall-free
   function (8,840 B / 2,210 insns).  Screen re-confirmed: 0 `handwritten
   instruction` markers, 0 %gp_rel, 0 `switchdata`, 0 non-$ra `jr` (no jump
   tables at all), and 0 bare-constant `($at)` displacements — every $at use is
   a gas address/compare macro.  It COMPILES and LINKS in its slot.

   State (compile-only masked shape diff, §D 2b; registers anchored for the
   "reg" figure, masked for the "structure" figure):

     first m2c decode   2202 insns, 827 reg / 247 structure over 149 regions, off -8
     now                2193 insns, 725 reg / 191 structure over 126 regions, off -17

   `make progress` scores it 344 / 8,840 partial bytes.  That number is NOT a
   measure of distance: partial credit is positional (§C), and the running
   offset leaves zero at orig[29] — the very first excursion — so every word
   after insn 29 scores nothing even though the offset is back to 0 by insn 33
   and stays within +-5 of zero for the next 1,270 instructions.

   THE HIGHEST-VALUE NEXT MOVE is therefore not the biggest region, it is the
   4-insn head knot at orig[28..50]: the original materialises `env0`
   (&g_abFrameDrawEnv0, s5) at insn 28 — between `VSync(0)` and the first
   PutDispEnv's argument load — and the scratch base (&g_pRenderScratchPrimTop,
   s0) at insn 34, with `addiu s2,s0,-8` filling PutDrawEnv's delay slot at 39.
   Ours emits both one call later.  Closing that alone is worth roughly 1,270
   words == ~5,000 partial bytes, because the whole first half is otherwise
   offset-neutral.

   Levers already applied (each measured; do not undo one without re-measuring):
     * A186 — `nGlyphs = K;` inside the cursor arm and `n = nGlyphs;` AFTER the
       `if`.  The original's `andi rX,rX,0xff` is a one-insn JOIN block that
       reorg duplicates into the `bne` delay slot; reading the count before the
       arm gives one `andi` instead of two.  Five sites.
     * A228 — two incomplete-array aliases carry the held-base pairs the
       original derives with an `addiu`:
         g_apRenderScratchPrimTopBlock (0x800785f0) -> [-2] is
           g_pRenderScratchRegionBase (`addiu s2,s0,-8`), and
         g_anHudFrameCycleBlock (0x80077fe8) -> [0x14b] is
           &g_anLevelSpriteTexWordPairs[2] (`addiu s8,s2,1324`),
         plus g_adwHudBobSinePhaseBlock (0x80077fe4) for the world-egg loop,
         whose preheader forms BOTH `s6 = s5+4` and `s5 = s5+1328`.
       The alias must be used INLINE — an intermediate pointer local (`top = …;
       top[-2]`) folds the -8 into the addressing mode and loses the `addiu`.
     * A240 per-site held bases — g_abLevelTotalDragonsBlock,
       g_abLevelTotalEggsBlock, g_anLevelGemsBlock, g_abWorldTitleGlyphBlock.
       The original addresses the SAME egg-count table absolutely at the `> 0`
       guard (`lui $at; addu $at,$at,v0; lbu v0,-2944($at)`) and off a held base
       at the `== 1` test and the loop condition, so the sized `extern` from
       globals.h and the incomplete-array alias are both in use, per site.
     * A113 — the cosine LUT is read `lh` in the eight glyph-wave loops but
       `lhu` at the two bob sites (`lhu; sll 16; sra 25` and `lhu; srl 8`);
       ((unsigned short *)g_anCosineLut)[…] buys the second form.
     * A158 — the fourth menu-border EmitRadialShadedLine is written with
       LITERALS in both substate arms; jump.c cross-jumps the shared `jal`.
       Routing it through shared x/y/n locals instead cost 3 `move`s.
     * A52 / A217 — every region got its own block-scoped scalars.  This is
       what removed the `bias` spill (it now lives in s8, the original uses s7)
       and took the register-anchored count 793 -> 734 in one edit.
     * A137 — `bx = bias + K;` named temps.  `scroll + (bias + K)` is
       reassociated by fold to `(scroll + K) + bias`; the original is
       `addiu v1,s7,K; addu v0,v0,v1`.  Five sites, 212 -> 204.
     * The two volume-bar loops read g_nPauseMenuCursor into a local BEFORE the
       four sprite-record field stores; the guard's load cannot hoist over
       stores through the record pointer, so source order decides it.

   Named residues, largest first (offsets are into the original's insn stream):
     R1  orig[28..50] — the head-knot above.  Positional only, 4 insns, but it
         owns ~5,000 partial bytes.  Not yet attacked.
     R2  orig[2012..2017] (-5) and orig[1900..1904] (-4) — the original
         RE-COMPUTES `g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i` from a fresh `lw` of the global
         inside the egg loop where we keep one cse'd address in a register
         (`move s2,v1`).  m2c's decode already says so: some sites read the
         global inline and some read a temp.  Needs the inline/temp split
         copied exactly, site by site, not a blanket temp.
     R3  orig[1700..1705] (-5), orig[1588..1591] (-3), orig[1472..1475] (-3) —
         same family: held-base/absolute choices inside the row loop that have
         not been walked site by site yet.
     R4  orig[150], orig[1317], orig[1428], orig[1646], orig[1688] (+3 each) —
         we emit three insns the original does not.  Unexamined.
     R5  the register map.  725 anchored vs 191 structure means ~530 of the
         residue is allocation.  The original keeps the repeated sprite-record
         store literals (0x7f, 0x0b, 0xff, 0x2e, 0x20, 0x18, 0x40) in
         callee-saved registers across the whole function (A133) — s0..s8 are
         mostly CONSTANTS in the original, which is the single biggest
         difference from our map.  Named locals for those literals is the
         obvious next experiment and has not been tried.

   Not a decode problem: there are no unresolved control-flow or content
   questions left in the body.  m2c's only complaint is the varargs $a3 artifact
   on the seven sprintf calls, which is expected. */

#include "globals.h"

extern void BuildRenderEntityLists(void);
extern void ComposeFrameScene(void);
extern void RasterizeEmitList(void);
extern void DrawActors(void);
extern void SetupFrameOT(void);
extern void DrawSync(int mode);
extern int VSync(int mode);
extern DISPENV *PutDispEnv(DISPENV *env);
extern void PutDrawEnv(void *env);
extern void *LinkOTPrimitives(int depth_max);
extern void DrawOTag(void *ot);
extern void StoreImage(RECT *r, void *dst);
extern void LoadImage(RECT *r, void *src);
extern void ConvertRGB15ToLuma8(void *buf, int count);
extern void AddPrimToOT(int prim);
extern void SetDrawMode(int prim, int dfe, int dtd, unsigned int tpage, RECT *tw);
extern void FillWord(void *dst, unsigned int value, int byte_count);
extern void EmitRadialShadedLine(int x0, int y0, int x1, int y1);
extern void EmitTexturedQuad(short *rect, int *uv, int *rgb);
extern void EnqueueBlinkingMarkerSprite(int *pos, unsigned int phase, int dir);
extern void EnqueuePendingSpritePrims(void);
extern void RasterizeSpritePrimQueue(void);
extern void EnqueueLoadingScreenSprites(void);
extern void *BuildTextSpriteChain(char *text, int *pos, int step, int flags);
extern void *BuildTextSprites(char *text, int *pos, int *style, int step, int flags);
extern int ComputeInventoryProgressPercent(void);
extern int strlen(char *s);
extern int sprintf(char *buf, char *fmt, ...);

/* Held-base alias for g_pRenderScratchPrimTop (0x800785f0);
   [-2] is g_pRenderScratchRegionBase. */
extern void *g_apRenderScratchPrimTopBlock[];
/* Held-base view of g_nVsyncFrameEndCount; [-1] = g_nVsyncFramePaceAnchor. */
extern int g_anVsyncFrameEndBlock[];
/* cosine view of the sine LUT (g_anSineLut + 0x80). */
extern short g_anCosineLut[];
/* Held-base alias for g_dwHudBobSinePhase (0x80077fe4): [1] is the mod-9 HUD
   frame counter and [0x14c] is &g_anLevelSpriteTexWordPairs[2]. */
extern int g_adwHudBobSinePhaseBlock[];
/* Same block seen from g_nHudFrameCycleMod9 (0x80077fe8): [0x14b] is
   &g_anLevelSpriteTexWordPairs[2]. */
extern int g_anHudFrameCycleBlock[];
/* Held-base (incomplete-array) views of four tables the inventory row loop
   keeps in one register each; the plain sized decls in globals.h stay in use
   at the sites the original addresses absolutely (A240). */
extern unsigned char g_abLevelTotalDragonsBlock[];
extern unsigned char g_abLevelTotalEggsBlock[];
extern int g_anLevelGemsBlock[];
extern unsigned char g_abWorldTitleGlyphBlock[];
/* menu label blobs that have no friendly name yet. */
extern char D_80010B24[]; /* "QUIT GAME?"  */
extern char D_80010B30[]; /* "SOUND FX"    */
extern char D_80010B40[]; /* "MUSIC"       */
extern char D_80010B50[]; /* "SOUND"       */
extern char D_80010B60[]; /* "VIBRATION"   */
extern char D_80010B6C[]; /* "CONTINUE"    */
extern char D_80010B78[]; /* "INVENTORY"   */
extern char D_80010B84[]; /* "EXIT LEVEL"  */
extern char D_80010B90[]; /* "EXIT WORLD"  */

/* Draw for gamestates 2 (pause menu), 3 (inventory) and 6 (dialog overlay)
   — 0x8001a40c, 8840 bytes.

   On the entry frame (g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames == 0) it renders one last
   full gameplay scene, then freezes it: StoreImage pulls the frame back out
   of VRAM, ConvertRGB15ToLuma8 packs it to 8bpp luma four 0x80-wide strips at
   a time, each strip is re-uploaded at x=0x200 and the gray CLUT is loaded at
   (0x200,0xe0).  Every later frame re-draws that backdrop as four textured
   quads, draws the menu on top, and submits the frame with the shared
   two-vblank pacing tail. */
void Gamestate02_03_06_Draw(void) {
  RECT rect;        /* sp18 */
  char buf[0x20];   /* sp20 */
  int pos[3];       /* sp40 */
  int styA[3];      /* sp50 */
  int styB[3];      /* sp60 */
  int styC[3];      /* sp70 */
  short quad[4];    /* sp80 */
  short quad2[4];   /* sp88 */
  int styD[3];      /* sp90 */
  unsigned char rows; /* spA0 */

  if (g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames == 0) {
    DRAWENV *env0;
    int i;
    int x;
    int y;
    int h;
    i = 0;
    BuildRenderEntityLists();
    h = 0xe0;
    ComposeFrameScene();
    x = 0x200;
    RasterizeEmitList();
    DrawActors();
    SetupFrameOT();
    DrawSync(0);
    VSync(0);
    env0 = &g_abFrameDrawEnv0;
    PutDispEnv((DISPENV *)((char *)g_pActiveFrameDrawEnv + 0x5c));
    PutDrawEnv(g_pActiveFrameDrawEnv);
    DrawOTag(LinkOTPrimitives(0x800));
    DrawSync(0);
    VSync(0);
    PutDispEnv((DISPENV *)((char *)g_pActiveFrameDrawEnv + 0x5c));
    rect.x = 0x200;
    rect.y = 0;
    rect.w = 0x100;
    rect.h = 0xe1;
    StoreImage(&rect,
               (void *)((char *)g_apRenderScratchPrimTopBlock[0] - 0x1c200));
    do {
      y = 8;
      rect.x = i << 7;
      if (g_pActiveFrameDrawEnv != env0) {
        y = 0xf8;
      }
      i++;
      rect.y = y;
      rect.w = 0x80;
      rect.h = h;
      StoreImage(&rect, g_apRenderScratchPrimTopBlock[-2]);
      DrawSync(0);
      ConvertRGB15ToLuma8(g_apRenderScratchPrimTopBlock[-2], 0x7000);
      rect.x = x;
      x += 0x40;
      rect.y = 0;
      rect.w = 0x40;
      rect.h = h;
      LoadImage(&rect, g_apRenderScratchPrimTopBlock[-2]);
    } while (i < 4);
    rect.x = 0x200;
    rect.y = 0xe0;
    rect.w = 0x20;
    rect.h = 1;
    LoadImage(&rect, g_anMenuBackdropGrayClut);
    DrawSync(0);
    g_nVsyncFramePaceAnchor = VSync(-1);
  } else {
    void *prim;
    int i;
    int x;
    int h;
    void *env = &g_abFrameDrawEnv0;
    if (g_pActiveFrameDrawEnv == &g_abFrameDrawEnv0) {
      env = (void *)((char *)env + 0x84);
    }
    i = 0;
    PutDrawEnv(env);
    g_nPrimBufferOverflowFlag = 0;
    g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor = g_pRenderScratchRegionBase;
    g_pPrimBufferLimit = (void *)((char *)g_pRenderScratchRegionBase + 0x1c000);
    g_pSpriteRecordBufferTop = (void *)((char *)g_pRenderScratchPrimTop - 0x1c200);
    g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor = (void *)((char *)g_pRenderScratchPrimTop - 0x1c200);
    x = i << 7;
    do {
      int clut = i + 0x88;
      prim = g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor;
      *((int *)prim) = 0x9000000;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 7)) = 0x2c;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 4)) = 0x4c;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 5)) = 0x80;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 8)) = x;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0xa)) = 8;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x10)) =
          *((unsigned short *)((int)prim + 8)) + 0x80;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x1a)) =
          *((unsigned short *)((int)prim + 0xa)) + 0xdf;
      i++;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xd)) = 0;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x12)) = *((unsigned short *)((int)prim + 0xa));
      h = 0x40;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xc)) = 0;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x18)) = *((unsigned short *)((int)prim + 8));
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x20)) =
          *((unsigned short *)((int)prim + 8)) + 0x80;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x22)) =
          *((unsigned short *)((int)prim + 0xa)) + 0xdf;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 6)) = h;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x15)) =
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xd));
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x1c)) =
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xc));
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x14)) =
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xc)) + 0x80;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x1d)) =
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xd)) - 0x21;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x24)) =
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xc)) + 0x80;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x25)) =
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0xd)) - 0x21;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0xe)) = 0x3820;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x16)) = clut;
      AddPrimToOT((int)prim);
      g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor = (void *)((int)prim + 0x28);
      x = i << 7;
    } while (i < 4);
    *((int *)((int)prim + 0x28)) = 0x3000000;
    *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x2f)) = h;
    *((short *)((int)prim + 0x30)) = 0;
    *((short *)((int)prim + 0x32)) = 0xe7;
    *((short *)((int)prim + 0x34)) = 0x200;
    *((short *)((int)prim + 0x36)) = 0xe7;
    *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x2c)) = 0;
    *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x2d)) = 0;
    *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x2e)) = 0;
    AddPrimToOT((int)prim + 0x28);
    g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor = (void *)((int)prim + 0x38);
    if (g_nGamestate == 2) {
      unsigned char *rec;
      short *lut;
      unsigned char nGlyphs;
      int cur;
      int n;
      int phase;
      int v;
      int y;
      void *box = (void *)((int)prim + 0x38);
      SetDrawMode((int)box, 1, 0, 0x40, (RECT *)0);
      AddPrimToOT((int)box);
      *((int *)((int)prim + 0x44)) = 0x5000000;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x4b)) = 0x2a;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x48)) = h;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x49)) = h;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x4a)) = h;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x4e)) = 0x43;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x52)) = 0x43;
      box = (void *)((int)prim + 0x44);
      if (g_nPauseMenuSubstate == 1) {
        *((short *)((int)prim + 0x4c)) = 0x54;
        *((short *)((int)prim + 0x50)) = 0x1ac;
        rows = g_nPadIsDualshockFlag != 0;
        y = rows * 0x10 + 0xb6;
      } else {
        rows = 1;
        *((short *)((int)prim + 0x4c)) = 0x8c;
        *((short *)((int)prim + 0x50)) = 0x174;
        y = 0xb0;
      }
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x56)) = y;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x5a)) = y;
      *((short *)((int)box + 0x10)) = *((unsigned short *)((int)box + 8));
      *((short *)((int)box + 0x14)) = *((unsigned short *)((int)box + 0xc));
      AddPrimToOT((int)box);
      g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor = (void *)((int)box + 0x18);
      EmitRadialShadedLine(0xe0, 0x61, 0x120, 0x61);
      if (g_nPauseMenuSubstate == 1) {
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x54, 0x43, 0x1ac, 0x43);
        v = rows * 0x10 + 0xb6;
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x1ac, 0x43, 0x1ac, v);
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x1ac, v, 0x54, v);
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x54, v, 0x54, 0x43);
      } else {
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x8c, 0x43, 0x174, 0x43);
        v = rows * 0x12 + 0x9e;
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x174, 0x43, 0x174, v);
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x174, v, 0x8c, v);
        EmitRadialShadedLine(0x8c, v, 0x8c, 0x43);
      }
      pos[0] = 0xba;
      pos[1] = 0x52;
      pos[2] = 0xc00;
      BuildTextSpriteChain(g_szUiPaused, pos, 0x1c, 0xb);
      if (g_nPauseMenuSubstate == 2) {
        styA[0] = 0x10;
        styA[2] = 0x1400;
        pos[0] = 0xb7;
        styA[1] = 1;
        pos[1] = 0x77;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        BuildTextSprites(D_80010B24, pos, styA, 0x12, 0xb);
        pos[0] = 0xc0;
        pos[1] = 0x94;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        BuildTextSprites(g_szUiYes, pos, styA, 0x12, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 0) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 3;
        }
        pos[0] = 0x128;
        pos[1] = 0x94;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        BuildTextSprites(g_szUiNo, pos, styA, 0x12, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 1) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 2;
        }
        n = nGlyphs;
        i = 0;
        if (n > 0) {
          lut = g_anCosineLut;
          phase = 0;
          do {
            i++;
            v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
            phase += 0xc;
            rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
            rec += 0x58;
          } while (i < n);
        }
      } else if (g_nPauseMenuSubstate == 1) {
        styB[0] = 0xf;
        styB[2] = 0x1600;
        styB[1] = 1;
        pos[0] = 0x6b;
        pos[1] = 0x6c;
        pos[2] = 0x1400;
        BuildTextSprites(D_80010B30, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 0) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 0xb;
        }
        pos[0] = 0x79;
        pos[1] = 0x7c;
        pos[2] = 0x1400;
        BuildTextSprites(D_80010B40, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 1) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 0xb;
        }
        pos[0] = 0x6b;
        pos[1] = 0x8c;
        pos[2] = 0x1400;
        BuildTextSprites(D_80010B50, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 2) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 0xc;
        }
        if (g_nPadIsDualshockFlag != 0) {
          pos[0] = 0xa3;
          pos[1] = 0x9c;
          pos[2] = 0x1400;
          BuildTextSprites(D_80010B60, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
          if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 3) {
            rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
            nGlyphs = 9;
          }
        }
        pos[0] = 0xd0;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        v = rows * 0x10;
        pos[1] = v + 0x9c;
        BuildTextSprites(g_szUiCamera, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 4) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 6;
        }
        pos[0] = 0xee;
        pos[1] = v + 0xac;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        BuildTextSprites(g_szUiDone, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 5) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 4;
        }
        n = nGlyphs;
        i = 0;
        if (n > 0) {
          lut = g_anCosineLut;
          phase = 0;
          do {
            i++;
            v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
            phase += 0xc;
            rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
            rec += 0x58;
          } while (i < n);
        }
        if (g_nSfxVolume == 0) {
          pos[0] = 0x142;
          pos[1] = 0x6c;
          pos[2] = 0x1400;
          BuildTextSprites(g_szUiOff, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
          phase = 0;
          if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 0) {
            rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
            i = 0;
            do {
              i++;
              v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
              phase += 0xc;
              rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
              rec += 0x58;
            } while (i < 3);
          }
        } else {
          i = 0;
          if (g_nSfxVolume > 0) {
            phase = 0;
            x = 0x140;
            do {
              rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor - 0x58;
              g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor = rec;
              FillWord(rec, 0, 0x58);
              cur = g_nPauseMenuCursor;
              *((short *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x36)) = 0x1b2;
              *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x10)) = 0x6d;
              *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0xc)) = x;
              *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x14)) = 0x1400;
              if (cur == 0) {
                *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) =
                    lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff] * 3 >>
                    9;
              } else {
                *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) = 0;
              }
              phase += 0xc;
              *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x47)) = 0x7f;
              *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x4f)) = 0xb;
              *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x50)) = 0xff;
              i++;
              x += 0xa;
            } while (i < g_nSfxVolume);
          }
        }
        if (g_nMusicVolume == 0) {
          pos[0] = 0x142;
          pos[1] = 0x7c;
          pos[2] = 0x1400;
          BuildTextSprites(g_szUiOff, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
          phase = 0;
          if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 1) {
            rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
            i = 0;
            do {
              i++;
              v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
              phase += 0xc;
              rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
              rec += 0x58;
            } while (i < 3);
          }
        } else {
          i = 0;
          if (g_nMusicVolume > 0) {
            phase = 0;
            x = 0x140;
            do {
              rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor - 0x58;
              g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor = rec;
              FillWord(rec, 0, 0x58);
              cur = g_nPauseMenuCursor;
              *((short *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x36)) = 0x1b2;
              *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x10)) = 0x7d;
              *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x14)) = 0x1400;
              *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0xc)) = x;
              if (cur == 1) {
                *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) =
                    lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff] * 3 >>
                    9;
              } else {
                *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) = 0;
              }
              phase += 0xc;
              *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x47)) = 0x7f;
              *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x4f)) = 0xb;
              *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x50)) = 0xff;
              i++;
              x += 0xa;
            } while (i < g_nMusicVolume);
          }
        }
        pos[0] = 0x142;
        pos[1] = 0x8c;
        pos[2] = 0x1400;
        if (g_nSoundMonoMixFlag != 0) {
          BuildTextSprites(g_szUiMono, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
          n = 4;
        } else {
          BuildTextSprites(g_szUiStereo, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
          n = 6;
        }
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 2) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          i = 0;
          if (n != 0) {
            phase = 0;
            do {
              i++;
              v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
              phase += 0xc;
              rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
              rec += 0x58;
            } while (i < n);
          }
        }
        if (g_nPadIsDualshockFlag != 0) {
          pos[0] = 0x142;
          pos[1] = 0x9c;
          pos[2] = 0x1400;
          if (g_nOptionVibrationEnabled != 0) {
            BuildTextSprites(g_szUiOn, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
            n = 2;
          } else {
            BuildTextSprites(g_szUiOff, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
            n = 3;
          }
          if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 3) {
            rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
            i = 0;
            if (n != 0) {
              phase = 0;
              do {
                i++;
                v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
                phase += 0xc;
                rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
                rec += 0x58;
              } while (i < n);
            }
          }
        }
        pos[0] = 0x142;
        pos[1] = rows * 0x10 + 0x9c;
        pos[2] = 0x1400;
        if (g_dwActiveCameraOptions == 2) {
          BuildTextSprites(g_szUiActive, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
          n = 6;
        } else {
          BuildTextSprites(g_szUiPassive, pos, styB, 0x10, 0xb);
          n = 7;
        }
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 4) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          i = 0;
          if (n != 0) {
            phase = 0;
            do {
              i++;
              v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
              phase += 0xc;
              rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
              rec += 0x58;
            } while (i < n);
          }
        }
      } else {
        styC[0] = 0x10;
        styC[2] = 0x1400;
        pos[0] = 0xc7;
        styC[1] = 1;
        pos[1] = 0x6e;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        BuildTextSprites(D_80010B6C, pos, styC, 0x12, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 0) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 8;
        }
        pos[0] = 0xcf;
        pos[1] = 0x80;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        BuildTextSprites(g_szUiOptions, pos, styC, 0x12, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 1) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 7;
        }
        pos[0] = 0xbf;
        pos[1] = 0x92;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        BuildTextSprites(D_80010B78, pos, styC, 0x12, 0xb);
        if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 2) {
          rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          nGlyphs = 9;
        }
        if (g_nFlightLevelActive != 0) {
          pos[0] = 0xe7;
          pos[1] = 0xa4;
          pos[2] = 0x1100;
          BuildTextSprites(g_szUiQuit, pos, styC, 0x12, 0xb);
          if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 3) {
            rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
            nGlyphs = 4;
          }
          n = nGlyphs;
        } else if (g_nActiveLevelId != g_nActiveLevelId / 10 * 10) {
          pos[0] = 0xb7;
          pos[1] = 0xa4;
          pos[2] = 0x1100;
          BuildTextSprites(D_80010B84, pos, styC, 0x12, 0xb);
          if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 3) {
            rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
            nGlyphs = 9;
          }
          n = nGlyphs;
        } else {
          pos[0] = 0xbf;
          pos[1] = 0xa4;
          pos[2] = 0x1100;
          BuildTextSprites(D_80010B90, pos, styC, 0x12, 0xb);
          if (g_nPauseMenuCursor == 3) {
            rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
            nGlyphs = 8;
          }
          n = nGlyphs;
        }
        i = 0;
        if (n > 0) {
          lut = g_anCosineLut;
          phase = 0;
          do {
            i++;
            v = lut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff];
            phase += 0xc;
            rec[0x46] = v * 3 >> 9;
            rec += 0x58;
          } while (i < n);
        }
      }
    } else if (g_nGamestate == 3) {
      unsigned char *rec;
      int n;
      int phase;
      int v;
      int y;
      int bx;
      int bx2;
      int pct = ComputeInventoryProgressPercent();
      int bias;
      pos[0] = 0x1b8;
      pos[1] = 0x2c;
      pos[2] = 0x900;
      if (pct >= 0xa) {
        pos[0] = 0x196;
      }
      if (pct >= 0x64) {
        pos[0] -= 0x22;
      }
      sprintf(buf, g_szFmtPercentD, pct);
      BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x22, 2);
      pos[0] = 0x1de;
      buf[0] = '%';
      buf[1] = 0;
      BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x22, 2);
      pos[0] = 0x5a;
      pos[1] = 0x24;
      pos[2] = 0xb40;
      sprintf(buf, g_szFmtPercentD, g_nWorldTreasureCollected);
      BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x1b, 2);
      pos[0] = 0x14d;
      pos[1] = 0x24;
      pos[2] = 0xb40;
      if (g_nWorldDragonsRescued >= 0xa) {
        pos[0] = 0x132;
      }
      sprintf(buf, g_szFmtPercentD, g_nWorldDragonsRescued);
      BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x1b, 2);
      rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor - 0x58;
      g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor = rec;
      FillWord(rec, 0, 0x58);
      *((short *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x36)) = 0x1d7;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0xc)) = 0x2e;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x10)) = 0x2e;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x14)) = 0xc00;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x45)) =
          ((unsigned short *)g_anCosineLut)[g_dwHudBobSinePhase] << 0x10 >> 0x19;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) =
          g_dwHudBobSinePhase;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x47)) = 0x7f;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x4f)) = 0xb;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x50)) = 0xff;
      rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor - 0x58;
      g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor = rec;
      FillWord(rec, 0, 0x58);
      *((short *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x36)) = 0x1fa;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0xc)) = 0x12c;
      if (g_nWorldDragonsRescued >= 0xa) {
        *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0xc)) = 0x111;
      }
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x10)) = 0x2e;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x14)) = 0x780;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) =
          ((unsigned short *)g_anCosineLut)[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 0x10 &
                                             0x1f0) >>
                                            1] >>
          8;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x47)) = 0x7f;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x4f)) = 0xb;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x50)) = 0xff;
      x = 0x24;
      if (g_nWorldEggsRecovered > 0) {
        i = 0;
        y = 0x18;
        do {
          int *uv;
          int *rgb;
          quad[1] = 0x32;
          quad[2] = 0x18;
          quad[0] = y;
          quad[3] = 0x10;
          if (i >= g_nWorldEggsRecovered) {
            pos[1] = 0x3a;
            pos[0] = x;
            pos[2] = 0x1800;
            BuildTextSpriteChain(g_szUiGlyphX, pos, 0, 2);
            uv = &g_anLevelSpriteTexWordPairs[2];
            rgb = pos;
            pos[0] = 0x20;
            pos[1] = 0x20;
            pos[2] = 0x20;
          } else {
            rgb = (int *)0;
            uv = &g_adwHudBobSinePhaseBlock[0x14c] +
                 (g_adwHudBobSinePhaseBlock[1] + i) % 9 * 2;
          }
          x += 0x1b;
          EmitTexturedQuad(quad, uv, rgb);
          i++;
          y += 0x1b;
        } while (i < 0xc);
      }
      EmitRadialShadedLine(0x40, 0x45, 0x1c0, 0x45);
      prim = g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor;
      SetDrawMode((int)prim, 1, 0, 0x40, (RECT *)0);
      AddPrimToOT((int)prim);
      *((int *)((int)prim + 0xc)) = 0x5000000;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x13)) = 0x2a;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x10)) = 0x60;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x11)) = 0x60;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x12)) = 0x60;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x16)) = 0x46;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x1a)) = 0x46;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x14)) = 0x40;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x18)) = 0x1c0;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x1c)) = 0x40;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x1e)) = 0x47;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x20)) = 0x1c0;
      *((short *)((int)prim + 0x22)) = 0x47;
      AddPrimToOT((int)prim + 0xc);
      g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor = (void *)((int)prim + 0x24);
      EmitRadialShadedLine(0x40, 0x47, 0x1c0, 0x47);
      n = g_nSubMenuCursor;
      if (n > 0 && g_abLevelVisitedFlagVirtualBase[n * 6] != 0) {
        pos[0] = 0x28;
        pos[1] = 0x48;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        EnqueueBlinkingMarkerSprite(pos, g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 2, 1);
      }
      if (n < 5 && (&g_abLevelVisitedFlag[6])[n * 6] != 0) {
        pos[0] = 0x1d7;
        pos[1] = 0x48;
        pos[2] = 0x1100;
        EnqueueBlinkingMarkerSprite(pos, g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 2, 0);
      }
      i = 0;
      bias = (g_nSubMenuCursor < 3) * 8;
      v = strlen((&g_apTitleCardNames[1])[g_nSubMenuCursor]);
      pos[1] = 0x5c;
      pos[2] = 0xe00;
      styD[0] = 0x14;
      styD[2] = 0x1000;
      styD[1] = 2;
      pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset - ((v - 1) * 0xa - 0x9e);
      BuildTextSprites((&g_apTitleCardNames[1])[g_nSubMenuCursor], pos, styD, 0x17,
                       2);
      rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
      phase = 0;
      if ((int)g_abWorldTitleGlyphBlock[g_nSubMenuCursor] > 0) {
        do {
          i++;
          rec[0x46] =
              g_anCosineLut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) & 0xff] *
                  3 >>
              9;
          phase += 0xc;
          rec += 0x58;
        } while (i < (int)g_abWorldTitleGlyphBlock[g_nSubMenuCursor]);
      }
      rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor - 0x58;
      g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor = rec;
      FillWord(rec, 0, 0x58);
      *((short *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x36)) = 0x1d7;
      bx = bias + 0x15a;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0xc)) =
          g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + bx;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x10)) = 0x6c;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x14)) = 0xc00;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x45)) =
          ((unsigned short *)g_anCosineLut)[g_dwHudBobSinePhase] << 0x10 >> 0x19;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) =
          g_dwHudBobSinePhase;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x47)) = 0x7f;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x4f)) = 0xb;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x50)) = 0xff;
      rec = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor - 0x58;
      g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor = rec;
      FillWord(rec, 0, 0x58);
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0xc)) =
          g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1d1;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x10)) = 0x6e;
      *((short *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x36)) = 0x1fa;
      *((int *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x14)) = 0x780;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x46)) =
          ((unsigned short *)g_anCosineLut)[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 0x10 &
                                             0x1f0) >>
                                            1] >>
          8;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x47)) = 0x7f;
      i = 0;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x4f)) = 0xb;
      y = 0x7b;
      *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x50)) = 0xff;
      do {
        if (g_abLevelVisitedFlag[g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i] != 0) {
          unsigned char *first;
          int *gems;
          int row;
          prim = g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor;
          SetDrawMode((int)prim, 1, 0, 0x40, (RECT *)0);
          AddPrimToOT((int)prim);
          *((int *)((int)prim + 0xc)) = 0x5000000;
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x13)) = 0x2a;
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x10)) = 0x28;
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x11)) = 0x28;
          *((unsigned char *)((int)prim + 0x12)) = 0x28;
          v = y - 0xa;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x16)) = v;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x1a)) = v;
          v = y + 9;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x1e)) = v;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x22)) = v;
          v = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1ff;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x14)) = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x18)) = v;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x1c)) = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset;
          *((short *)((int)prim + 0x20)) = v;
          AddPrimToOT((int)prim + 0xc);
          h = y - 0xb;
          g_pPrimBufferWriteCursor = (void *)((int)prim + 0x24);
          EmitRadialShadedLine(g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x70, h,
                               g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0xd0, h);
          bx = bias + 0x13a;
          bx2 = bias + 0x17a;
          EmitRadialShadedLine(g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + bx, h,
                               g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + bx2, h);
          EmitRadialShadedLine(g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1ae, h,
                               g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1ee, h);
          styD[0] = 0x10;
          styD[1] = 1;
          styD[2] = 0x1400;
          pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x24;
          pos[1] = y;
          pos[2] = 0x1100;
          first = (unsigned char *)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor;
          BuildTextSprites(g_apLevelNameStrings[g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i], pos,
                           styD, 0x12, 2);
          bx = bias + 0x113;
          x = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + bx;
          gems = &g_anLevelGemsBlock[g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i];
          pos[0] = x;
          if (*gems < 0x3e8) {
            pos[0] = x + 0x12;
          }
          if (*gems < 0x64) {
            pos[0] += 0x12;
          }
          if (*gems < 0xa) {
            pos[0] += 0x12;
          }
          sprintf(buf, g_szFmtPercentD, *gems);
          BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x12, 2);
          pos[2] = 0x1800;
          bx = bias + 0x15a;
          pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + bx;
          BuildTextSpriteChain(g_szUiSlash, pos, 0x12, 2);
          pos[2] = 0x1100;
          bx = bias + 0x16b;
          pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + bx;
          sprintf(buf, g_szFmtPercentD,
                  g_anLevelTotalGemsTable[g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i]);
          BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x12, 2);
          row = g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i;
          if (g_abLevelTotalDragonsBlock[row] != 0) {
            pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1bd;
            sprintf(buf, g_szFmtPercentD, g_anLevelDragonsRescued[row]);
            BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x12, 2);
            pos[2] = 0x1800;
            pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1ce;
            BuildTextSpriteChain(g_szUiSlash, pos, 0x12, 2);
            pos[2] = 0x1100;
            pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1df;
            sprintf(buf, g_szFmtPercentD,
                    g_abLevelTotalDragonsBlock[g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i]);
            BuildTextSpriteChain(buf, pos, 0x12, 2);
          } else {
            pos[2] = 0x1800;
            pos[0] = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1ce;
            BuildTextSpriteChain(g_szUiSlash, pos, 0x12, 2);
            *((unsigned char *)((int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor + 0x44)) = 0x29;
          }
          if (g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i == g_nLevelIntroIndex) {
            rec = first - 0x58;
            if ((int)rec >= (int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor) {
              phase = 0;
              do {
                rec[0x46] =
                    g_anCosineLut[(g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames * 8 + phase) &
                                  0xff] *
                        3 >>
                    9;
                rec -= 0x58;
                phase += 0xc;
              } while ((int)rec >= (int)g_pSpriteRecordWriteCursor);
            }
          }
          if (g_nWorldEggsRecovered > 0) {
            n = g_nSubMenuCursor;
            if (n < 3) {
              int e = 0;
              if ((int)g_abLevelTotalEggsTable[n * 6 + i] > 0) {
                int ex = 0;
                do {
                  int *uv;
                  int *rgb;
                  int gx = g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0xe8 + ex;
                  int gx2 = gx;
                  if (g_abLevelTotalEggsBlock[n * 6 + i] == 1) {
                    gx2 = gx + 0x18;
                  }
                  quad2[1] = y - 8;
                  quad2[2] = 0x18;
                  quad2[0] = gx2;
                  quad2[3] = 0x10;
                  if (e >= g_anLevelEggsRecovered[g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i]) {
                    pos[0] = gx2 + 0xc;
                    pos[1] = y;
                    pos[2] = 0x1800;
                    BuildTextSpriteChain(g_szUiGlyphX, pos, 0, 2);
                    uv = &g_anLevelSpriteTexWordPairs[2];
                    rgb = pos;
                    pos[0] = 0x20;
                    pos[1] = 0x20;
                    pos[2] = 0x20;
                  } else {
                    rgb = (int *)0;
                    uv = &g_anHudFrameCycleBlock[0x14b] +
                         (g_anHudFrameCycleBlock[0] + i) % 9 * 2;
                  }
                  ex += 0x18;
                  EmitTexturedQuad(quad2, uv, rgb);
                  e++;
                } while (e < (int)g_abLevelTotalEggsBlock[g_nSubMenuCursor * 6 + i]);
              }
            }
          }
          y += 0x13;
        }
        i++;
        h = y - 0xb;
      } while (i < 6);
      EmitRadialShadedLine(g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x70, h,
                           g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0xd0, h);
      EmitRadialShadedLine(g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x140, h,
                           g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x180, h);
      EmitRadialShadedLine(g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1ae, h,
                           g_nSubMenuScrollOffset + 0x1ee, h);
    }
    g_apSpritePrimQueue[0] = (void *)0;
    if (g_nGamestate == 2 && g_nFlightLevelActive == 0) {
      EnqueueLoadingScreenSprites();
    }
    EnqueuePendingSpritePrims();
    FillWord(&g_pOtDepthBinHead0, 0, 0x900);
    RasterizeSpritePrimQueue();
    DrawOTag(LinkOTPrimitives(0));
    DrawSync(0);
    if (g_nDeathRespawnPending != 0) {
      VSync(0);
    }
    g_nVsyncFrameEndCount = VSync(-1);
    if (g_nVsyncFrameEndCount - g_nVsyncFramePaceAnchor < 2) {
      int *end = g_anVsyncFrameEndBlock;
      do {
        VSync(0);
        g_nVsyncFrameEndCount = VSync(-1);
      } while (g_nVsyncFrameEndCount - end[-1] < 2);
    }
    g_nVsyncFramePaceAnchor = VSync(-1);
    PutDispEnv((DISPENV *)((char *)g_pActiveFrameDrawEnv + 0x5c));
  }
  g_nPauseMenuTransitionFrames++;
}
